# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
#
# Only content-addressed paths are listed: package_<hash>/ changes with every build and
# every _framework/ file carries a fingerprint in its name, so both can be cached forever.
# Everything else (index.html, service-worker.js, manifest.webmanifest) keeps the Pages
# default of revalidating on every request. That default matters: deployments are atomic,
# so a stale index.html would point at a package_<hash>/ the new deployment no longer has.
#
# Rules that match the same request have their values joined with a comma, so don't add a
# catch-all /* Cache-Control rule here. The deploy workflow appends a noindex rule for
# the staging and preview slots.

/_framework/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/package_*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
